### OrderQuery — Phase 1, Query Definition & Simulation (design-time)
### Focused on two things: param validation (declaring params, missing/wrong-typed params at
### simulate time) and the drafted vs. non-drafted distinction (what /engine/drafted returns
### before a draft exists, while one is open, and after it's gone via discard/publish).
### A query is one row of the table qe_stored_query, in one of three states: drafted -> simulated ->
### published. There is no versioning: drafting a queryName again overwrites its row (and clears
### "simulated"), and a published query must be taken offline on purpose to be edited (step 8a).
### Everything is in Postgres -- there is no in-memory state to lose on a restart.
###
### Content types: /engine/draft accepts and returns application/json. /engine/draft-yml is a
### separate endpoint for the same operation that accepts application/yaml and returns
### application/json (see request 1b). Every other /engine endpoint is JSON-only.
###
### Prereqs: order-query is running (./dry-run.sh, or ./gradlew :order-query:bootRun) against a
### fresh database (./stop.sh then ./dry-run.sh resets it; otherwise it picks up where it left off).
###
### Run requests TOP TO BOTTOM in a single pass — later ones depend on state left by earlier ones.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@queryName = orders.ordersByStatusAndBranch
@author = senior_dba@bracits.com

### 0a. Query roles — the realm roles + groups catalog the UI offers at publish time (to choose
### allowed_roles) and at run time (to pick a calling identity). From query-engine.roles in application.yml,
### or the engine's built-in demo catalog when none is configured.
GET {{baseUrl}}/query-roles

### 0. Drafted (resume) — 404 DRAFT_NOT_FOUND. Non-drafted: queryName has never been drafted.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/drafted
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}"
}

### 1. Draft — validates the entry and opens a draft for queryName, stored with state drafted.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/draft
Content-Type: application/json
X-Author: {{author}}

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}",
  "sql": "SELECT orderId, status, total, branchId FROM order_projection WHERE status = :status AND branchId = :branchId",
  "params": { "status": "String", "branchId": "int" }
}

### 1b. Draft — separate endpoint, /engine/draft-yml, body is application/yaml, response is
### still application/json. Overwrites the draft opened in step 1 with the same content.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/draft-yml
Content-Type: application/yaml
X-Author: {{author}}

queryName: orders.ordersByStatusAndBranch
sql: "SELECT orderId, status, total, branchId FROM order_projection WHERE status = :status AND branchId = :branchId"
params:
  status: String
  branchId: int

### 1c. Draft with a param validation error — :branchId is used in sql but missing from
### params. Stored as status=DRAFT (not VALIDATED); the draft is kept even though validation failed.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/draft
Content-Type: application/json
X-Author: {{author}}

{
  "queryName": "orders.orderById",
  "sql": "SELECT orderId FROM order_projection WHERE orderId = :orderId",
  "params": {}
}

### 2. Drafted (resume) — drafted case. Reads back the open draft for queryName from step 1b
### without changing anything. Useful after a browser crash/new tab, per the PRD.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/drafted
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}"
}

### 3. Simulate — param validation: 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT, missing the required "branchId" param.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/simulate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}",
  "params": { "status": "SHIPPED" }
}

### 3a. Simulate — param validation: 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT, "branchId" has the wrong type
### (string instead of int).
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/simulate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}",
  "params": { "status": "SHIPPED", "branchId": "not-a-number" }
}

### 4. Simulate — happy path. Executes against the real projection store and marks the draft
### as simulated (required before publish).
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/simulate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}",
  "params": { "status": "SHIPPED", "branchId": 12 }
}

### 4a. Simulate — 422 DRAFT_INVALID. orders.orderById is still status=DRAFT (param validation
### error from step 1c), so it can't be simulated yet.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/simulate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queryName": "orders.orderById",
  "params": { "orderId": "O-1001" }
}

### 5. Publish — 422 NOT_SIMULATED. orders.orderById was never successfully simulated
### (see 4a), so publish is refused. allowed_roles (realm roles and/or group names from
### /query-roles) are supplied here at publish time, not during drafting.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/publish
Content-Type: application/json
X-Author: {{author}}

{
  "queryName": "orders.orderById",
  "allowed_roles": ["senior_DBA"]
}

### 6. Discard — releases the never-publishable orders.orderById draft from steps 1c/4a/5.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/discard
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queryName": "orders.orderById"
}

### 6a. Drafted (resume) — non-drafted case again: 404 DRAFT_NOT_FOUND. orders.orderById's
### draft was just discarded, so it's back to "never drafted" from the caller's point of view.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/drafted
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queryName": "orders.orderById"
}

### 7. Publish — happy path. queryName was simulated in step 4, so this succeeds and moves the
### row to state published. allowed_roles mixes a realm role
### (senior_DBA) and a group (data-platform); both are enforced by name at invoke time.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/publish
Content-Type: application/json
X-Author: {{author}}

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}",
  "allowed_roles": ["senior_DBA", "data-platform"]
}

### 7a. Drafted (resume) — 404 DRAFT_NOT_FOUND. queryName is published, not a draft, so there is
### nothing to resume (see /engine/list for a view of every query and its state).
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/drafted
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}"
}

### 8. Draft over a published query — 409 QUERY_PUBLISHED. A live query is never taken offline by
### accident: drafting it again needs "unpublish": true.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/draft
Content-Type: application/json
X-Author: {{author}}

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}",
  "sql": "SELECT orderId, status, total, branchId FROM order_projection WHERE status = :status AND branchId = :branchId",
  "params": { "status": "String", "branchId": "int" }
}

### 8a. ... with "unpublish": true it is accepted. The query goes back to state drafted and is OFFLINE
### until it is simulated and published again. The response has previouslyPublished: true and the
### roles chosen last time in allowedRoles.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/draft
Content-Type: application/json
X-Author: {{author}}

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}",
  "sql": "SELECT orderId, status, total, branchId FROM order_projection WHERE status = :status AND branchId = :branchId",
  "params": { "status": "String", "branchId": "int" },
  "unpublish": true
}

### 8b. A caller now gets 409 QUERY_NOT_PUBLISHED ("being edited"), not a 404.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: senior_DBA

{
  "name": "{{queryName}}",
  "params": { "status": "SHIPPED", "branchId": 12 }
}

### 8c. A different author tries to draft the same queryName and gets 409 DRAFT_LOCKED (the holder
### is named in the message). The draft stays locked until its holder publishes or discards it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/draft
Content-Type: application/json
X-Author: another.dba@bracits.com

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}",
  "sql": "SELECT orderId, status, total, branchId FROM order_projection WHERE status = :status AND branchId = :branchId",
  "params": { "status": "String", "branchId": "int" },
  "unpublish": true
}

### 9. Simulate again (the edit cleared "simulated") ...
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/simulate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}",
  "params": { "status": "SHIPPED", "branchId": 12 }
}

### 9a. ... and publish again: the query is live again. (Discard instead would delete it
### completely, because the row is the only copy.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/publish
Content-Type: application/json
X-Author: {{author}}

{
  "queryName": "{{queryName}}",
  "allowed_roles": ["senior_DBA", "data-platform"]
}

### 10. Draft — 400 INVALID_QUERY_NAME. Name isn't in "{module}.{name}" form.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/draft
Content-Type: application/json
X-Author: {{author}}

{
  "queryName": "badname",
  "sql": "SELECT 1",
  "params": {}
}

### 11. List — one item per query with its single state: queryName is published here (published set,
### draft: null). A query being edited would have published: null and a draft with its state.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/list
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 11a. List — filtered to the orders module and PUBLISHED status only.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/list
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "filter": { "module": "orders", "status": ["PUBLISHED"] },
  "page": { "size": 50 }
}
